routing.sprint-design-critic:
# AGENTS

When the design has been scored and the taste questions are answered:
  @Engineering Manager, please lock the architecture and write the test matrix.

routing.sprint-design-partner:
# AGENTS

When the direction and the system are drafted:
  @Design Critic, please score it against the rubric and improve the two weakest dimensions.

routing.sprint-dx-lead:
# AGENTS

When shortening the path would need a scope decision:
  @Product Visionary, please decide it rather than letting the review assume an answer.

routing.sprint-eng-manager:
# AGENTS

When the architecture is settled and the first-run path is now visible:
  @Developer Experience Lead, please measure the time to a first working result and trace the friction.

routing.sprint-product-visionary:
# AGENTS

When the scope is settled and the surface needs a direction:
  @Design Partner, please set the design direction before anyone scores it.

routing.sprint-investigation-lead:
# AGENTS

When the cause is located, or three attempts have failed:
  @Staff Reviewer, please decide whether the fix belongs in this change or its own.

routing.sprint-second-opinion:
# AGENTS

When the two verdicts disagree on something with a real consequence:
  @Staff Reviewer, please settle it against the evidence rather than by seniority.

routing.sprint-security-officer:
# AGENTS

When a finding needs the exact code path traced before it can be confirmed:
  @Investigation Lead, please trace it so the finding is verified rather than suspected.

routing.sprint-staff-reviewer:
# AGENTS

When the review is written and the change is consequential enough to need a second read:
  @Second Opinion Reviewer, please reach your own verdict before reading mine.
When something fails and the cause is not obvious from the change:
  @Investigation Lead, please find the cause before anyone proposes a fix.
When the change touches input handling, identity, permissions or stored data:
  @Security Officer, please run the security pass against the new surface.

routing.sprint-founder-partner:
# AGENTS

When the problem is framed and the premises are accepted:
  @Product Visionary, please decide how big this should be and offer each expansion separately.

routing.sprint-product-visionary:
# AGENTS

When the scope is settled and finished has been defined:
  @Spec Author, please write the specification against the code that exists.

routing.sprint-spec-author:
# AGENTS

When reading the code contradicts a premise the brief depends on:
  @Founder Partner, please re-open that premise before the specification goes any further.
When the specification cannot be written without a scope decision nobody made:
  @Product Visionary, please make that call rather than letting the specification assume one.

routing.sprint-design-critic:
# AGENTS

When the design is settled and the change is implemented:
  @Staff Reviewer, please review it for what the suite does not catch.

routing.sprint-doc-engineer:
# AGENTS

When the documentation reveals that what shipped is not what was framed:
  @Founder Partner, please decide whether the framing or the product is the thing to change.

routing.sprint-founder-partner:
# AGENTS

When the problem is framed and the surface needs an honest score:
  @Design Critic, please score it and improve the weakest dimension directly.

routing.sprint-qa-lead:
# AGENTS

When the findings are fixed and each fix has its regression test:
  @Release Engineer, please take it to a green, revertable release.

routing.sprint-release-engineer:
# AGENTS

When the release is prepared and the change alters what the product does:
  @Documentation Engineer, please correct the stale documents and write the missing one.

routing.sprint-staff-reviewer:
# AGENTS

When the review is done and the flows need walking:
  @QA Lead, please walk them end to end and classify what breaks.
